  "headline": "Soybeans gain 3.2% on the week; cattle and hogs rise too",
  "lead": "Jan soybeans settled Friday at $12.31½, up 37¾ cents on the week. Corn added only 4 cents. Beans did the lifting while the other grains stood nearly still, and that gap is what a bushel of beans earned this week.",
  "teaser": "Beans, cattle and hogs all finished the week higher; corn and wheat barely moved.",
  "one_number": {
    "value": "489,000",
    "unit": "hogs killed Friday, USDA estimate",
    "context": "That is 4,000 more than a week ago, and cattle slaughter was 106,000 head, up from 93,000. Packers are running steady on both."
